\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y+4(0)y=0\\,⇒\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, one equilibrium is $(0,0).$\n\n- If $y=\\frac{2}{3},$ substituting it into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y+4xy & =0 \\\\ y(-5+4x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}(-5+4x) & =0 \\\\ -5+4x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero equilibrium of the model is\n$(\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{2}{3}).$" 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186179693 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496238 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186179715 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496244 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186179715 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496284 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186184197 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496298 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186198349 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496264 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186198354 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496282 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186198405 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496295 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186198433 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496297 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495684 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216585 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495684 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495585 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216586 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495585 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496029 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216591 1078 #edb/ref 17592186496029 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216592 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495617 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216592 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495617 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216593 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496012 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216593 1078 #edb/ref 17592186496012 13194139535324 17592186045417 true] [17592186216594 1075 #edb/ref 17592